# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
node_modules/
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
.next/
out/

# production
build/

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...but the example must be in version control: it is the only record of
# which variables the application needs.
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# use pnpm; npm lockfile is not tracked
package-lock.json

# Prisma client, generated on install (see database/prisma/schema.prisma)
database/generated/
# The query engine, staged into the app so a deployed function can find
# it (see apps/web/scripts/stage-prisma-engine.mjs). Build output.
apps/web/generated/
# Playwright CLI output (may contain credentials)
.playwright-cli/
.next-build

# Internal audit documents. Kept on disk, deliberately NOT published.
#
# This repository is public. These files are security and billing audits of a
# live deployment that takes real payments: they name unremediated findings in
# the present tense, and they carry NOT VERIFIED and BLOCKED markers against
# specific mechanisms. Written for the operator they are a remediation plan;
# published on a public repository they are also a list of what is not fixed
# yet.
#
# Not a secret and not a deletion: the content is in the working tree and the
# full history is on the local branch backup/pre-docs-filter. If the repository
# is ever made private, or the open items are closed, remove these two lines
# and commit them.
#
# docs/security/README.md is NOT ignored -- it predates this and is already
# published.
docs/security/PRODUCTION_SECURITY_AUDIT.md
docs/security/SECURITY_REMEDIATION_PLAN.md
docs/testing/
docs/performance/FINAL_PERFORMANCE_AUDIT.md
docs/deployment/PRODUCTION_GO_LIVE_CHECKLIST.md

# Agent tooling. Skills vendored from other people's repositories, the lockfile
# that pins them, local plugin settings, and the artefacts of design runs. None
# of it is the application, and .agents/ alone is 3.8MB of third-party text.
.agents/
.claude/
.hallmark/
skills-lock.json
